# Electron process rules

- Keep `contextIsolation: true`, `nodeIntegration: false`, and `sandbox: true`.
- Renderer APIs belong in `electron/preload.cjs` as named functions only.
- Use `packages/contracts/ipc-channels.cjs` for channel names. Do not invent ad-hoc channels.
- Validate privileged IPC payloads with `packages/contracts/ipc-validation.cjs` before acting.
- Window, tray and notification code stays in `electron/main.cjs`. Native actions still go through registered tools.

```javascript
// ❌ BAD
ipcMain.handle('run', (_e, cmd) => require('child_process').exec(cmd))

// ✅ GOOD
ipcMain.handle(IPC.agentMessage, async (_e, payload) => agent.handle(parseAgentMessage(payload).message))
```
